[B1] PASS global mass is constant to round-off over 2000 steps of the divergence with one flux per face and closed walls: on 512 cells of a gnomonic-equiangular panel the relative mass drift is +5.869e-20 per step and -1.265e-16 over the run, against a sequential-reduction bound of 5.673e-14 and a machine epsilon of 2.220e-16. The face terms cancel exactly between neighbours, so what is left is the rounding of the reduction and of the update, not transport
[B2] PASS global total energy, stored energy plus potential, is constant to round-off over 2000 steps when the gravity work is booked at the faces: on 512 cells the relative drift of sum (E + rho phi) V is -4.151e-19 per step and -1.644e-16 over the run, against the reduction bound 5.673e-14. The face booking moves each parcel of mass across the potential of the face it crosses, so the work terms telescope with the mass terms that produced them
[B3] PASS the six panels' solid angles sum to 4 pi and their volumes to the shell's, and the discrete divergence of r rhat is 3: at 12 by 12 cells per panel the solid angles sum to +0.00e+00 of 4 pi and the volumes to +0.00e+00 of 4 pi (ro^3 - ri^3) / 3; max |div(r rhat) - 3| is 3.24e-14 over all 6912 cells. Every volume-weighted budget below rests on these three numbers: a volume measure that is not the exact radial integral of the same solid angle as the x1 face area makes a conserved total drift with the grid rather than with the flow
[B4] PASS a uniform-pressure state at rest feels no tangential force on the cubed sphere, so it exerts no spurious axial torque: over all 6 panels at 8 by 8 by 6 cells the largest covariant tangential force density is 2.472e-17 against a single term of size 1.350e-02, i.e. 1.83e-15 relative; the global axial torque is -5.960e-08 N m against 5.891e+09 N m of unsigned torque. The cancellation is exact by construction: x_ov_rD is the discrete difference of the SAME product, face area times sine, that the x2 pressure flux divides by the volume, so only the order of the two multiplications differs
[B5] PASS global axial angular momentum stays at round-off over 2000 steps of the uniform-pressure rest state: over 2304 cells on 6 panels the drift is +5.482e-08 kg m^2 s^-1 per step and +1.831e-04 over the run, which is +8.72e-34 and +2.91e-30 of the 6.284e+25 kg m^2 s^-1 the same cells would carry at one metre per second eastward, against a bound of 1e-20 per step. The source of the drift is the rounding of the two multiplication orders in [B4] and nothing else: there is no term left over for it to accumulate. The bound is set to separate this from the same operator DELETED on all six panels, which drifts at 2.1e-18 per step -- sixteen orders worse, and still inside the 1e-15 this claim used to ask for
